ment that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule"],"id":"long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 1.2 (realising finite monotone witness rules)","locator":"Long record Proposition 1.2, p. 13, label prop:257-finite-witness-rule","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $E$ be a finite set of primes, and let $\\mathcal U$ be an upward-closed family of subsets of $E$ with $E\\in\\mathcal U$ and $\\varnothing\\notin\\mathcal U$. There is a set $A_{\\mathcal U}\\subseteq\\mathbb N_{>0}$ with $\\sum_{a\\in A_{\\mathcal U}}1/a=\\infty$ such that, for every integer $b\\ge2$ and every finite set $\\mathcal P$ of primes,\n$$\n\n\n W_{b,\\mathcal P}(A_{\\mathcal U})<\\infty\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad \\mathcal P\\cap E\\in\\mathcal U.\n$$\nMoreover $X_B(b)$ is irrational for every infinite $B\\subseteq A_{\\mathcal U}$ and every integer $b\\ge2$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.finite_monotone_witness_rule_realised%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.finite_monotone_witness_rule_realised%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lea